# Build context for the production image (see Dockerfile). The context is the
# repository root, so this file is the only thing standing between the build and the
# whole working tree.
#
# Two jobs, in order of importance:
#   1. leak guards — .env files, private keys and the secrets directory must never
#      reach a layer (threat T-02-03). A leaked layer cannot be patched afterwards.
#   2. context hygiene — node_modules, stale dist and internal planning material are
#      platform-specific or private, and shipping them only inflates the image and
#      poisons pnpm's store with foreign .bin shims and native modules.
#
# NOT ignored, deliberately: `apps/api/prisma/migrations`. The runtime stage copies
# `prisma/` out of the build stage, so ignoring it would produce an image with no
# migration history while every other check stayed green. Kept explicit here because
# a future "tidy up" pass is exactly what would drop it.

node_modules
**/node_modules

**/dist

.git
.github

.planning

# The App manifest tree is consumed by Supervisor, not by the image build.
homeweave_app

# Internal docs and examples never ship.
docs
examples

# Second line of defence behind `sourceMap: false` in apps/api/tsconfig.json:
# a source map embeds sourcesContent, which leaks the sources in another form.
*.map

**/*.spec.ts
**/*.test.*
**/__tests__

.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets
